preConditionHook:
// GRIMES'S NAMED PULLBACK TEMPLATE (Buying Support / Shorting Resistance,
// G06-21), the book's central trend-continuation trade, carried as the book
// states it and with its parts INLINED, as the corpus does for a named setup.
// Grimes treats flags, pennants, wedges and continuation triangles as
// functionally identical, so there are no per-shape variants.
//
// FOUR PARTS:
//   1. A STRONG SETUP LEG (ExtensionLegExceedsSetupLeg, G06-14): the leg
//      running now -- from swing-low occurrence 1 up to this closing price --
//      is at least extensionRatio times the same-direction leg before it.
//   2. A QUIET PULLBACK (PullbackRangeBelowLegRange, G06-15): the mean bar
//      range over the last pullbackBars bars is below reducedFraction of the
//      mean bar range of the legBars bars immediately before them.
//   3. NOT THREE TESTS OF ITS OWN SUPPORT (PullbackSupportTestCount, G06-16,
//      which merge priority D maps onto LevelTouchCount at minTouches 3): the
//      pullback's support has been touched and held FEWER than maxSupportTests
//      times. Stated positively here, since the template ANDs it.
//   4. AN ENTRY TRIGGER: break-and-recover of the pullback's own extreme
//      (LevelBreakAndRecover, G06-03) **OR** a bounce off it
//      (SupportResistanceBounceEntry, G06-04 -- a merge working name found in
//      no slice, traced through the mined candidate to the on-disk
//      LowTouchesRecentRangeLow at lag 0, whose row records exactly that
//      mapping). THIS OR IS WHY THE TEMPLATE IS ONE FILE.
//
// THE PULLBACK'S SUPPORT IS SHARED STATE, which is the other reason this is one
// file: parts 3 and 4 read the same shifted pullbackLookback window extreme
// (merge decision 7's default level -- a confirmed pivot is only needed when a
// level must persist from a break to a later retest, and this one need not).
// TWO SHIFTS ARE KEPT APART on purpose: the break-and-recover reads the window
// ending TWO bars ago, so the breaking bar's own low cannot define the level it
// is said to have broken (LevelBreakAndRecover's spelling), while the touch
// count and the bounce read the window ending ONE bar ago
// (LowTouchesRecentRangeLow's spelling). THE LEVEL IS THE PULLBACK'S OWN, not a
// swing pivot, which is a stated departure from LevelTouchCount's construction
// for part 3 -- the D mapping was made on the COUNTER, not on the level, and
// G06-16 says "tests of support IN A PULLBACK".
//
// SIDES: the long buys support in an uptrend. Every part's long side is the
// support side, so unlike BreakoutBaseEntryTemplate there is no side-exchange
// obstruction here -- what panes cannot reach is the OR in part 4.
//
// MEASURED SWING PIVOT (decision 14, EL_Swing_Probe.txt): occurrences 1 and 2
// only, since occurrence 3+ is UNMEASURED; the pivot test is MIXED -- AT OR
// BEYOND the swingStrength OLDER bars, STRICTLY BEYOND the swingStrength NEWER
// bars -- the confirmation lag is exactly swingStrength bars, pivotLookback is
// EL's Length with offsets 0..pivotLookback-1, and an empty window returns the
// -1 SENTINEL, GUARDED ON THE BAR INDEX and never on the returned price.
// THE ORDERING GUARD is ExtensionLegExceedsSetupLeg's, LegOneEqualsLegTwoTarget's
// in origin: bars-ago counts must descend loBar2 > hiBar1 > loBar1 on the long
// side and the setup leg must actually be up (setupUp > 0, a price DIFFERENCE
// and so shift-safe), or an interleaved pivot pair would compare two unrelated
// legs.
//
// For GUARDS at >= 1 on all three loops: EasyLanguage's For counts DOWN when
// the end value is below the start, so `for kk = 0 to -1` would read the NEXT
// bar and `for kk = 1 to 0` the current one, where the C++ for-loops would not
// run at all. The means are guarded against a zero divisor the same way. Grids
// start at 1.
//
// SHIFT TEST: leg lengths and bar ranges are price DIFFERENCES, tolerances are
// ATR fractions, tests are a COUNT.
//
// WFSafe_AvgTrueRange is MultiWalk's ROLLING accumulator, a different function
// from the built-in it resembles.
//
// Deepest bar touched: max(pivotLookback - 1 + swingStrength,
// pullbackBars + legBars - 1, pullbackLookback + 1, atrLength + 1).
//
// THE C++ TWIN WRITES OUT BY HAND what the EL twin says with built-ins.
// Highest/Lowest bottom out in Extremes(), EL SOURCE, so each window is a scan
// SEEDED ON THE WINDOW'S FIRST BAR and continued with a STRICT comparison under
// the EL relational tolerance (el_gt / el_lt), which keeps a tie on the EARLIEST
// bar. The pivot scan is ExtensionLegExceedsSetupLeg's inlined form, written
// WITHOUT break and with the < 2 counters so occurrences 1 and 2 land in the
// same slots the EL twin's Occurrence arguments do.
//
// Every scratch value is a localVariables entry rather than a hook-scope
// declaration, so the hooks survive a double placement; loop counters and
// per-candidate flags are block-scoped inside their loops.
if (atrLenState != (int)atrLength) {
    atrSum = 0.0;
    for (int aa = 0; aa < (int)atrLength; ++aa) {
        hiV = high[aa] > close[aa + 1] ? high[aa] : close[aa + 1];
        loV = low[aa] < close[aa + 1] ? low[aa] : close[aa + 1];
        atrSum += hiV - loV;
    }
    atrLenState = (int)atrLength;
} else {
    outIdx = (int)atrLength;
    hiV = high[0] > close[1] ? high[0] : close[1];
    loV = low[0] < close[1] ? low[0] : close[1];
    hiO = high[outIdx] > close[outIdx + 1] ? high[outIdx] : close[outIdx + 1];
    loO = low[outIdx] < close[outIdx + 1] ? low[outIdx] : close[outIdx + 1];
    atrSum += hiV - loV;
    atrSum -= hiO - loO;
}
atrValue = atrSum / (int)atrLength;
nHi = 0;
nLo = 0;
hiPx1 = -1.0;
hiBar1 = -1.0;
hiPx2 = -1.0;
hiBar2 = -1.0;
loPx1 = -1.0;
loBar1 = -1.0;
loPx2 = -1.0;
loBar2 = -1.0;
for (int j = (int)swingStrength; j <= (int)pivotLookback - 1; ++j) {
    bool okHi = true;
    bool okLo = true;
    for (int k = j - (int)swingStrength; k < j; ++k) {
        if (!el_gt(high[j], high[k])) okHi = false;
        if (!el_lt(low[j], low[k])) okLo = false;
    }
    for (int k = j + 1; k <= j + (int)swingStrength; ++k) {
        if (!el_ge(high[j], high[k])) okHi = false;
        if (!el_le(low[j], low[k])) okLo = false;
    }
    if (okHi && nHi < 2) {
        nHi = nHi + 1;
        if (nHi == 1) { hiPx1 = high[j]; hiBar1 = (double)j; }
        if (nHi == 2) { hiPx2 = high[j]; hiBar2 = (double)j; }
    }
    if (okLo && nLo < 2) {
        nLo = nLo + 1;
        if (nLo == 1) { loPx1 = low[j]; loBar1 = (double)j; }
        if (nLo == 2) { loPx2 = low[j]; loBar2 = (double)j; }
    }
}
setupUp = hiPx1 - loPx2;
runUp = close[0] - loPx1;
setupDn = hiPx2 - loPx1;
runDn = hiPx1 - close[0];
legUp = (loBar1 != -1.0) && (loBar2 != -1.0) && (hiBar1 != -1.0)
    && el_gt(loBar2, hiBar1) && el_gt(hiBar1, loBar1) && el_gt(setupUp, 0.0)
    && el_ge(runUp, extensionRatio * setupUp);
legDn = (hiBar1 != -1.0) && (hiBar2 != -1.0) && (loBar1 != -1.0)
    && el_gt(hiBar2, loBar1) && el_gt(loBar1, hiBar1) && el_gt(setupDn, 0.0)
    && el_ge(runDn, extensionRatio * setupDn);
pbSum = 0.0;
for (int kk = 0; kk <= (int)pullbackBars - 1; ++kk) {
    pbSum = pbSum + (high[kk] - low[kk]);
}
legSum = 0.0;
for (int kk = (int)pullbackBars; kk <= (int)pullbackBars + (int)legBars - 1; ++kk) {
    legSum = legSum + (high[kk] - low[kk]);
}
pbMean = 0.0;
legMean = 0.0;
if ((int)pullbackBars >= 1) pbMean = pbSum / (int)pullbackBars;
if ((int)legBars >= 1) legMean = legSum / (int)legBars;
quiet = el_lt(pbMean, reducedFraction * legMean);
supp1 = low[1];
res1 = high[1];
for (int i = 2; i <= (int)pullbackLookback; ++i) {
    if (el_lt(low[i], supp1)) supp1 = low[i];
    if (el_gt(high[i], res1)) res1 = high[i];
}
supp2 = low[2];
res2 = high[2];
for (int i = 3; i <= (int)pullbackLookback + 1; ++i) {
    if (el_lt(low[i], supp2)) supp2 = low[i];
    if (el_gt(high[i], res2)) res2 = high[i];
}
testLo = 0;
testHi = 0;
for (int kk = 1; kk <= (int)pullbackLookback; ++kk) {
    if (el_le(low[kk], supp1 + tolAtr * atrValue) && el_gt(close[kk], supp1 - tolAtr * atrValue)) {
        testLo = testLo + 1;
    }
    if (el_ge(high[kk], res1 - tolAtr * atrValue) && el_lt(close[kk], res1 + tolAtr * atrValue)) {
        testHi = testHi + 1;
    }
}
trigUp = (el_lt(low[1], supp2) && el_gt(close[0], supp2)) || el_le(low[0], supp1 + tolAtr * atrValue);
trigDn = (el_gt(high[1], res2) && el_lt(close[0], res2)) || el_ge(high[0], res1 - tolAtr * atrValue);
